    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d570-a2">

                <pb facs="0802" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg696"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Reid to Sir E. Grey.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-08-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 16,
                    1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the letter
                    of Sir E. Gorst of August 14, regretting that, owing to the wide divergence from
                    your views disclosed in Mr. Root’s letter respecting the rights of American
                    vessels on the Newfoundland coast, it is hopeless to expect an immediate
                    settlement.</p>
                <p>I am glad to note that under these circumstances you expect soon to submit
                    proposals for a modus vivendi for the ensuing season, and shall hasten to advise
                    my Government of this purpose.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitelaw Reid.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
